<title>BELGIUM: EU confirms four green rate devaluations.</title>
<headline>EU confirms four green rate devaluations.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The green rates of the Belgian franc, German mark, Dutch guilder and Austrian schilling will be devalued with effect from Thursday, the European Commission confirmed.</p>
<p>The Belgian franc green rate will devalue to 40.3103 per Ecu, from 40.2147, the mark rate to 1.95540, from 1.95076, the guilder to 2,19663, from 2.19067 and the schilling to 13.7562, from 13.7246.</p>
<p>The UK's Home Grown Cereals Authority (HGCA) earlier on Wednesday forecast the devaluations, which follow changes on Tuesday, saying they were a result of the relative strength of the Finnish mark.</p>
</text>
